# Genius Developers Main - Workflow Analysis

This document provides a comprehensive analysis of the project structure, data flow, and operational workflows of the Genius Developers portfolio platform.

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

The application is built using a modern **Next.js 15+ (App Router)** architecture with a decoupled backend integrated via Next.js API Routes.

### Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: Next.js 15, React 19, Tailwind CSS 4, Framer Motion, Lucide Icons.
- **Backend**: Next.js API Routes (Edge/Node.js runtime).
- **Database**: MongoDB with Mongoose ODM.
- **Authentication**: JWT-based (using `jose`) with HTTP-only cookies.
- **UI Components**: Custom Shadcn/UI integration.

---

## 🔄 System Workflows

### 1. Authentication Flow
The admin panel is protected by a password-based authentication system.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant AdminLogin as /admin/login
    participant AuthAPI as /api/auth/login
    participant Cookie as HTTP-only Cookie
    
    User->>AdminLogin: Enters Password
    AdminLogin->>AuthAPI: POST { password }
    AuthAPI->>AuthAPI: Compare with process.env.ADMIN_PASSWORD
    alt Success
        AuthAPI-->>Cookie: Set "admin-token" (JWT)
        AuthAPI-->>AdminLogin: { success: true }
        AdminLogin-->>User: Redirect to /admin
    else Failure
        AuthAPI-->>AdminLogin: { error: "Invalid credentials" }
        AdminLogin-->>User: Show Error Toast
    end
```

### 2. Data Management Workflow (Admin)
Each module (Projects, Skills, etc.) follows a standard CRUD pattern.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph Admin Dashboard
        A[Sidebar Selection] --> B[Module Page]
        B --> C[Fetch List API]
        B --> D[Open Modal/Form]
        D --> E[Submit Form API]
    end
    
    subgraph API Layer
        C --> F[GET /api/admin/...]
        E --> G[POST/PUT /api/admin/...]
    end
    
    subgraph Database
        F --> H[(MongoDB)]
        G --> H
    end
    
    H -- Response --> B
```

### 3. Public Content Delivery
The homepage dynamically renders content managed in the admin panel.

1. **Request**: User visits `https://geniusdevelopers.space/`
2. **Server-Side Fetch**: `app/page.tsx` fetches data (Projects, Skills, Services) from the database.
3. **Hydration**: React 19 hydrates the components on the client.
4. **Interactivity**: Framer Motion handles entrance animations and smooth transitions.

